(window.DSA_TOPIC=window.DSA_TOPIC||{})["trees"]={"id":"trees","theory":"\n<h3>What it is</h3>\n<p>A <b>binary tree</b> is a node with up to two children, <code>left</code> and <code>right</code>, each itself a binary tree. Almost every tree problem is solved by asking: <i>if I already knew the answer for my left and right subtrees, how would I combine them?</i></p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">class TreeNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, left=None, right=None):\n        self.val, self.left, self.right = val, left, right</code></pre>\n<p>A <b>binary search tree (BST)</b> adds a rule: everything in the left subtree is smaller than the node, everything in the right is larger. So an inorder walk gives sorted order, and search takes O(h) where h is the height (log n if balanced, n if it degenerates into a line).</p>\n<h3>Traversals</h3>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Order</th><th>Visit</th><th>Used for</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Preorder</td><td>node, left, right</td><td>copying / serialising a tree, path from root</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Inorder</td><td>left, node, right</td><td>BST → sorted order, k-th smallest, validate BST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Postorder</td><td>left, right, node</td><td>heights, diameters, anything that needs children first</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Level order (BFS)</td><td>row by row with a queue</td><td>levels, right side view, min depth, zigzag</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Spot the pattern</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Height / depth / diameter / balanced / max path\" → postorder DFS that <b>returns</b> one value and updates a global best.</li>\n<li>\"Per level\" → BFS with <code>for _ in range(len(queue))</code>.</li>\n<li>\"Root-to-node path\" or \"carry info downward\" (max so far, bounds) → pass it as a parameter.</li>\n<li>BST + \"find / k-th / validate / LCA\" → use the ordering to go left or right only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Template: postorder that returns height</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">def height(node):\n    if not node:\n        return 0\n    l, r = height(node.left), height(node.right)\n    # combine here: update a global answer with l, r\n    return 1 + max(l, r)</code></pre>\n<h3>Common mistakes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Validating a BST only against the direct parent instead of the full (low, high) range.</li>\n<li>Forgetting the <code>None</code> base case.</li>\n<li>Deep recursion on skewed trees: Python's default limit is 1000 frames — use an explicit stack if n can be large.</li>\n</ul>\n","qs":{"binary-tree-inorder-traversal":{"statement":"Return the inorder traversal (left, node, right) of a binary tree.","examples":[["root = [1, None, 2, 3]","[1, 3, 2]"],["root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, 8, None, None, 6, 7, 9]","[4, 2, 6, 5, 7, 1, 3, 9, 8]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [4, 2, 6, 1, 3, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Recursive DFS: visit left, record the node, visit right.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h) call stack","code":"def inorder_traversal(root):\n    res = []\n\n    def dfs(node):\n        if node:\n            dfs(node.left)\n            res.append(node.val)\n            dfs(node.right)\n    dfs(root)\n    return res"},"opt":{"idea":"Same order with an explicit stack: push the whole left spine, pop and record, then move to the right child. (Morris traversal reaches O(1) space.)","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def inorder_traversal(root):\n    res, stack, cur = [], [], root\n    while cur or stack:\n        while cur:\n            stack.append(cur)\n            cur = cur.left\n        cur = stack.pop()\n        res.append(cur.val)\n        cur = cur.right\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Pop 1 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[2],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["4","2"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 2 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2,1],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["4"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 3 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[2,1,3],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["4"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 4 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[2,1,3,0],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":[],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 5 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[2,1,3,0,5],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["6"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 6 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[2,1,3,0,5,4],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":[],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[2,1,3,0,5,4],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":[],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"maximum-depth-of-binary-tree":{"statement":"Return the number of nodes on the longest root-to-leaf path.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","3"],["root = [1, None, 2]","2"],["root = []","0"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","brute":{"idea":"List every root-to-leaf path and take the longest.","tc":"O(n · h)","sc":"O(n · h)","code":"def max_depth(root):\n    paths = []\n\n    def walk(node, path):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        path = path + [node.val]\n        if not node.left and not node.right:\n            paths.append(path)\n        walk(node.left, path)\n        walk(node.right, path)\n    walk(root, [])\n    return max((len(p) for p in paths), default=0)"},"opt":{"idea":"depth(node) = 1 + max(depth(left), depth(right)); an empty tree has depth 0.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def max_depth(root):\n    def depth(node):\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        d = 1 + max(depth(node.left), depth(node.right))\n        return d\n    return depth(root)","frames":[{"m":"depth(9) = 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(15) = 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(7) = 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(20) = 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(3) = 3","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"invert-binary-tree":{"statement":"Mirror a binary tree: swap every node's left and right children.","examples":[["root = [4, 2, 7, 1, 3, 6, 9]","[4, 7, 2, 9, 6, 3, 1]"],["root = [2, 1, 3]","[2, 3, 1]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [4, 2, 7, 1, 3, 6, 9]","brute":{"idea":"Build a brand-new mirrored copy of the tree.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n) new nodes","code":"def invert_tree(root):\n    if not root:\n        return None\n    return TreeNode(root.val, invert_tree(root.right), invert_tree(root.left))"},"opt":{"idea":"At every node swap left and right, then invert both subtrees in place.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def invert_tree(root):\n    top = root\n\n    def inv(node):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        node.left, node.right = node.right, node.left\n        inv(node.left)\n        inv(node.right)\n    inv(root)\n    return root","frames":[{"m":"Swap the children of 4","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 7","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 9","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 6","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 2","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 3","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 1","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: [4, 7, 2, 9, 6, 3, 1]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"same-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if two binary trees have the same shape and values.","examples":[["p = [1, 2, 3], q = [1, 2, 3]","True"],["p = [1, 2], q = [1, None, 2]","False"],["p = [1, 2, 1], q = [1, 1, 2]","False"]],"vizIn":"p = [1, 2, 3, 4], q = [1, 2, 3, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Serialise both trees with None markers and compare the strings.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def is_same_tree(p, q):\n    def ser(n):\n        return \"#\" if not n else f\"({n.val},{ser(n.left)},{ser(n.right)})\"\n    return ser(p) == ser(q)"},"opt":{"idea":"Recurse on both trees together: both empty → True; one empty or values differ → False; else compare left with left and right with right.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_same_tree(p, q):\n    rp, rq = p, q\n\n    def same(a, b):\n        if not a and not b:\n            return True\n        if not a or not b or a.val != b.val:\n            return False\n        return same(a.left, b.left) and same(a.right, b.right)\n    return same(p, q)","frames":[{"m":"Both 1 — compare children","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Both 2 — compare children","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Mismatch: 4 vs 5","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: False","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"symmetric-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if the tree is a mirror of itself around its centre.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 3]","True"],["root = [1, 2, 2, None, 3, None, 3]","False"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 3]","brute":{"idea":"Make an inverted copy and check it equals the original.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def is_symmetric(root):\n    def mirror(n):\n        return None if not n else TreeNode(n.val, mirror(n.right), mirror(n.left))\n\n    def same(a, b):\n        if not a or not b:\n            return a is b\n        return a.val == b.val and same(a.left, b.left) and same(a.right, b.right)\n    return same(root, mirror(root))"},"opt":{"idea":"Compare the left subtree with the right subtree mirrored: outer pair (a.left, b.right) and inner pair (a.right, b.left).","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_symmetric(root):\n    def mirror(a, b):\n        if not a or not b:\n            return a is b\n        return a.val == b.val and mirror(a.left, b.right) and mirror(a.right, b.left)\n    return mirror(root.left, root.right)","frames":[{"m":"Compare 2 with its mirror 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1,4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Compare 3 with its mirror 3","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2,6],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Compare 4 with its mirror 4","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":2},"binary-tree-level-order-traversal":{"statement":"Return the node values level by level, left to right.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","[[3], [9, 20], [15, 7]]"],["root = [1]","[[1]]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Find the height, then for each depth d run a DFS that collects nodes at depth d.","tc":"O(n · h)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def level_order(root):\n    def height(n):\n        return 0 if not n else 1 + max(height(n.left), height(n.right))\n\n    def collect(n, d, out):\n        if not n:\n            return\n        if d == 0:\n            out.append(n.val)\n        collect(n.left, d - 1, out)\n        collect(n.right, d - 1, out)\n    res = []\n    for d in range(height(root)):\n        row = []\n        collect(root, d, row)\n        res.append(row)\n    return res"},"opt":{"idea":"BFS with a queue; process exactly len(queue) nodes per round — that's one level.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(w) — widest level","code":"def level_order(root):\n    from collections import deque\n    if not root:\n        return []\n    res, q = [], deque([root])\n    while q:\n        level = []\n        for _ in range(len(q)):\n            node = q.popleft()\n            level.append(node.val)\n            if node.left:\n                q.append(node.left)\n            if node.right:\n                q.append(node.right)\n        res.append(level)\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Level 0: [3]","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":["9","20"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 1: [9, 20]","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[1,2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":["15","7"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3],[9,20]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 2: [15, 7]","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3],[9,20],[15,7]]"]]}]},{"m":"Result: [[3], [9, 20], [15, 7]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3],[9,20],[15,7]]"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"diameter-of-binary-tree":{"statement":"Return the number of edges on the longest path between any two nodes.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","3"],["root = [1, 2]","1"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, None, 6, None, None, 7]","brute":{"idea":"For every node, compute left and right heights with separate calls.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def diameter_of_binary_tree(root):\n    def height(n):\n        return 0 if not n else 1 + max(height(n.left), height(n.right))\n\n    def best(n):\n        if not n:\n            return 0\n        return max(height(n.left) + height(n.right), best(n.left), best(n.right))\n    return best(root)"},"opt":{"idea":"One postorder pass: each node returns its height, and left + right height through it is a candidate diameter.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def diameter_of_binary_tree(root):\n    best = 0\n\n    def height(node):\n        nonlocal best\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        l, r = height(node.left), height(node.right)\n        best = max(best, l + r)\n        return 1 + max(l, r)\n\n    height(root)\n    return best","frames":[{"m":"At 6: left height 0 + right height 0 = 0","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","0"]]}]},{"m":"At 4: left height 1 + right height 0 = 1","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","1"]]}]},{"m":"At 7: left height 0 + right height 0 = 0","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","1"]]}]},{"m":"At 5: left height 0 + right height 1 = 1","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","1"]]}]},{"m":"At 2: left height 2 + right height 2 = 4","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]},{"m":"At 3: left height 0 + right height 0 = 0","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]},{"m":"At 1: left height 3 + right height 1 = 4","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]}]},"tests":2},"balanced-binary-tree":{"statement":"A tree is height-balanced if every node's subtrees differ in height by at most 1. Check it.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","True"],["root = [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, None, None, 4, 4]","False"],["root = []","True"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","brute":{"idea":"At every node compare the heights of both subtrees, computing heights from scratch.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_balanced(root):\n    def height(n):\n        return 0 if not n else 1 + max(height(n.left), height(n.right))\n    if not root:\n        return True\n    return abs(height(root.left) - height(root.right)) <= 1 and is_balanced(root.left) and is_balanced(root.right)"},"opt":{"idea":"Return the height bottom-up, or −1 as soon as any subtree is unbalanced — the −1 short-circuits upward.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_balanced(root):\n    def check(node):\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        l, r = check(node.left), check(node.right)\n        if l < 0 or r < 0 or abs(l - r) > 1:\n            return -1\n        return 1 + max(l, r)\n    return check(root) >= 0","frames":[{"m":"9: heights 0 and 0 → height 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}}]},{"m":"15: heights 0 and 0 → height 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[3],"p":{}}]},{"m":"7: heights 0 and 0 → height 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[4],"p":{}}]},{"m":"20: heights 1 and 1 → height 2","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]},{"m":"3: heights 1 and 2 → height 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"subtree-of-another-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if <code>subRoot</code> appears as a full subtree of <code>root</code>.","examples":[["root = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2], sub = [4, 1, 2]","True"],["root = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2, None, None, None, None, 0], sub = [4, 1, 2]","False"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2], sub = [4, 1, 2]","brute":{"idea":"For every node of root, check whether the tree starting there equals subRoot.","tc":"O(m · n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_subtree(root, sub):\n    def same(a, b):\n        if not a or not b:\n            return a is b\n        return a.val == b.val and same(a.left, b.left) and same(a.right, b.right)\n    if not root:\n        return False\n    return same(root, sub) or is_subtree(root.left, sub) or is_subtree(root.right, sub)"},"opt":{"idea":"Serialise both trees in preorder with markers for None and delimiters around values; subRoot is a subtree exactly when its string is a substring. (Use KMP for a guaranteed linear search.)","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(m + n)","code":"def is_subtree(root, sub):\n    def ser(node, out):\n        if not node:\n            out.append(\"#\")\n            return\n        out.append(f\"^{node.val}\")\n        ser(node.left, out)\n        ser(node.right, out)\n\n    a, b = [], []\n    ser(root, a)\n    ser(sub, b)\n    big, small = \",\".join(a), \",\".join(b)\n    return small in big","frames":[{"m":"Preorder strings with # for None","l":13,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"root","v":[["3",1,4],["4",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"subRoot","v":[["4",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["root","^3,^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#,^5,#,#"],["subRoot","^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#"],["found","T"]]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"root","v":[["3",1,4],["4",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"subRoot","v":[["4",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["root","^3,^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#,^5,#,#"],["subRoot","^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#"],["found","T"]]}]}]},"tests":2},"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-search-tree":{"statement":"Return the lowest node in the BST that has both <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> as descendants (a node counts as its own descendant).","examples":[["root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, None, None, 3, 5], p = 2, q = 8","6"],["root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, None, None, 3, 5], p = 2, q = 4","2"],["root = [2, 1], p = 2, q = 1","2"]],"vizIn":"root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, None, None, 3, 5], p = 3, q = 5","brute":{"idea":"Use the general binary-tree LCA that ignores the ordering and searches both sides.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def lca_bst(root, p, q):\n    def lca(n):\n        if not n or n.val in (p.val, q.val):\n            return n\n        l, r = lca(n.left), lca(n.right)\n        return n if l and r else l or r\n    return lca(root)"},"opt":{"idea":"Walk from the root: both values smaller → go left; both larger → go right; otherwise this node is where they split — the LCA.","tc":"O(h)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def lca_bst(root, p, q):\n    node = root\n    while node:\n        if p.val < node.val and q.val < node.val:\n            node = node.left\n        elif p.val > node.val and q.val > node.val:\n            node = node.right\n        else:\n            return node","frames":[{"m":"At 6: p = 3, q = 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 2: p = 3, q = 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 4: p = 3, q = 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree":{"statement":"Return the lowest common ancestor of nodes <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> in a binary tree (no ordering).","examples":[["root = [3, 5, 1, 6, 2, 0, 8, None, None, 7, 4], p = 5, q = 1","3"],["root = [3, 5, 1, 6, 2, 0, 8, None, None, 7, 4], p = 5, q = 4","5"],["root = [1, 2], p = 1, q = 2","1"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 5, 1, 6, 2, 0, 8, None, None, 7, 4], p = 7, q = 8","brute":{"idea":"Record the root-to-p and root-to-q paths, then take the last node they share.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    def path(n, target, acc):\n        if not n:\n            return False\n        acc.append(n)\n        if n is target or path(n.left, target, acc) or path(n.right, target, acc):\n            return True\n        acc.pop()\n        return False\n    a, b = [], []\n    path(root, p, a)\n    path(root, q, b)\n    i = 0\n    while i < min(len(a), len(b)) and a[i] is b[i]:\n        i += 1\n    return a[i - 1]"},"opt":{"idea":"Each call returns p or q if it finds one below it. The first node that gets a non-empty answer from both sides is the LCA.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    top = root\n\n    def lca(node):\n        if not node or node is p or node is q:\n            return node\n        left, right = lca(node.left), lca(node.right)\n        if left and right:\n            return node\n        return left or right\n    return lca(root)","frames":[{"m":"At 6: left reports None, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 4: left reports None, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 2: left reports 7, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 5: left reports None, right reports 7","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 0: left reports None, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[7],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 1: left reports None, right reports 8","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 3: left reports 7, right reports 8","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"validate-binary-search-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if the tree is a valid BST (strictly smaller on the left, strictly larger on the right, all the way down).","examples":[["root = [2, 1, 3]","True"],["root = [5, 1, 4, None, None, 3, 6]","False"],["root = [5, 4, 6, None, None, 3, 7]","False"]],"vizIn":"root = [2, 1, 3]","brute":{"idea":"For every node, check that all values in its left subtree are smaller and all in its right are larger.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_valid_bst(root):\n    def vals(n):\n        return [] if not n else vals(n.left) + [n.val] + vals(n.right)\n    if not root:\n        return True\n    if any(v >= root.val for v in vals(root.left)) or any(v <= root.val for v in vals(root.right)):\n        return False\n    return is_valid_bst(root.left) and is_valid_bst(root.right)"},"opt":{"idea":"Pass an allowed (low, high) range down: going left tightens high to the node's value, going right tightens low.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_valid_bst(root):\n    def ok(node, low, high):\n        if not node:\n            return True\n        good = low < node.val < high\n        if not good:\n            return False\n        return ok(node.left, low, node.val) and ok(node.right, node.val, high)\n    return ok(root, float(\"-inf\"), float(\"inf\"))","frames":[{"m":"2 must be in (-inf, inf) → OK","l":5,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]},{"m":"1 must be in (-inf, 2) → OK","l":5,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}}]},{"m":"3 must be in (2, inf) → OK","l":5,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst":{"statement":"Return the k-th smallest value (1-indexed) in a BST.","examples":[["root = [3, 1, 4, None, 2], k = 1","1"],["root = [5, 3, 6, 2, 4, None, None, 1], k = 3","3"]],"vizIn":"root = [5, 3, 6, 2, 4, None, None, 1], k = 4","brute":{"idea":"Collect the full inorder list and index it.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    def ino(n):\n        return [] if not n else ino(n.left) + [n.val] + ino(n.right)\n    return ino(root)[k - 1]"},"opt":{"idea":"Iterative inorder visits values in sorted order; stop at the k-th pop.","tc":"O(h + k)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    stack, cur, count = [], root, 0\n    while True:\n        while cur:\n            stack.append(cur)\n            cur = cur.left\n        cur = stack.pop()\n        count += 1\n        if count == k:\n            return cur.val\n        cur = cur.right","frames":[{"m":"Inorder visit #1: 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","1"]]}]},{"m":"Inorder visit #2: 2","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","2"]]}]},{"m":"Inorder visit #3: 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","3"]]}]},{"m":"Inorder visit #4: 4","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","4"]]}]}]},"tests":2},"binary-tree-right-side-view":{"statement":"Return the values visible from the right side, top to bottom.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3, None, 5, None, 4]","[1, 3, 4]"],["root = [1, 2, 3, 4, None, None, None, 5]","[1, 3, 4, 5]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, None, 5, None, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Level-order traversal storing every level, then take each level's last value.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def right_side_view(root):\n    levels, q = [], [root] if root else []\n    while q:\n        levels.append([n.val for n in q])\n        q = [c for n in q for c in (n.left, n.right) if c]\n    return [lv[-1] for lv in levels]"},"opt":{"idea":"DFS visiting right before left; the first node reached at each new depth is the visible one.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def right_side_view(root):\n    res = []\n\n    def dfs(node, depth):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        if depth == len(res):\n            res.append(node.val)\n        dfs(node.right, depth + 1)\n        dfs(node.left, depth + 1)\n\n    dfs(root, 0)\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"First node at depth 0 (coming from the right): 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"First node at depth 1 (coming from the right): 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[0,3],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1","3"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"First node at depth 2 (coming from the right): 4","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[0,3,4],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 3, 4]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[0,3,4],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"construct-binary-tree-from-preorder-and-inorder-traversal":{"statement":"Build the tree from its preorder and inorder traversals (values are unique).","examples":[["preorder = [3, 9, 20, 15, 7], inorder = [9, 3, 15, 20, 7]","[3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]"],["preorder = [-1], inorder = [-1]","[-1]"]],"vizIn":"preorder = [3, 9, 20, 15, 7], inorder = [9, 3, 15, 20, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Take preorder[0] as the root, search for it in inorder to split, and slice lists for each side.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(n²) slices","code":"def build_tree(preorder, inorder):\n    if not preorder:\n        return None\n    root = TreeNode(preorder[0])\n    i = inorder.index(preorder[0])\n    root.left = build_tree(preorder[1:i + 1], inorder[:i])\n    root.right = build_tree(preorder[i + 1:], inorder[i + 1:])\n    return root"},"opt":{"idea":"Same split, but look up the root's inorder index in a dict and recurse on index ranges instead of slices.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def build_tree(preorder, inorder):\n    where = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(inorder)}\n    pre = iter(preorder)\n    holder = {}\n\n    def build(lo, hi):\n        if lo > hi:\n            return None\n        val = next(pre)\n        node = TreeNode(val)\n        holder.setdefault(\"root\", node)\n        node.left = build(lo, where[val] - 1)\n        node.right = build(where[val] + 1, hi)\n        return node\n\n    return build(0, len(inorder) - 1)","frames":[{"m":"Root 3 splits inorder[0..4] at index 1","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4],"ok":[1],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 9 splits inorder[0..0] at index 0","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 20 splits inorder[2..4] at index 3","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[2,3,4],"ok":[3],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 15 splits inorder[2..2] at index 2","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[2],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 7 splits inorder[4..4] at index 4","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[4],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[4],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":2},"binary-tree-maximum-path-sum":{"statement":"A path goes along parent–child edges and need not pass through the root. Return the largest sum of node values on any non-empty path.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3]","6"],["root = [-10, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","42"],["root = [-3]","-3"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3]","brute":{"idea":"Treat every node as the top of the path and compute the best downward chains from it with separate calls.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def max_path_sum(root):\n    def down(n):\n        return 0 if not n else max(0, n.val + max(down(n.left), down(n.right)))\n\n    def best(n):\n        if not n:\n            return float(\"-inf\")\n        through = n.val + down(n.left) + down(n.right)\n        return max(through, best(n.left), best(n.right))\n    return best(root)"},"opt":{"idea":"Each call returns the best chain going down from the node (dropping negative branches). The path through the node is val + left gain + right gain; keep the max.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def max_path_sum(root):\n    best = float(\"-inf\")\n\n    def gain(node):\n        nonlocal best\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        l = max(gain(node.left), 0)\n        r = max(gain(node.right), 0)\n        best = max(best, node.val + l + r)\n        return node.val + max(l, r)\n\n    gain(root)\n    return best","frames":[{"m":"Path through 2: 2 + 0 + 0 = 2","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","2"],["returns_up","2"]]}]},{"m":"Path through 3: 3 + 0 + 0 = 3","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","3"],["returns_up","3"]]}]},{"m":"Path through 1: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","6"],["returns_up","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 6","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","6"],["returns_up","4"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"serialize-and-deserialize-binary-tree":{"statement":"Design <code>serialize(root) → str</code> and <code>deserialize(str) → root</code> so that the tree round-trips exactly.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]","[1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]"],["root = []","[]"],["root = [1, None, 2, None, 3]","[1, None, 2, None, 3]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Store the tree as an array using heap positions (children of i at 2i+1, 2i+2). A skewed tree of n nodes needs about 2ⁿ slots.","tc":"O(2ⁿ) worst","sc":"O(2ⁿ) worst","code":"class Codec:\n    def serialize(self, root):\n        slots = {}\n\n        def put(n, i):\n            if n:\n                slots[i] = n.val\n                put(n.left, 2 * i + 1)\n                put(n.right, 2 * i + 2)\n        put(root, 0)\n        size = max(slots) + 1 if slots else 0\n        return \",\".join(str(slots[i]) if i in slots else \"#\" for i in range(size))\n\n    def deserialize(self, data):\n        if not data:\n            return None\n        vals = data.split(\",\")\n\n        def get(i):\n            if i >= len(vals) or vals[i] == \"#\":\n                return None\n            return TreeNode(int(vals[i]), get(2 * i + 1), get(2 * i + 2))\n        return get(0)"},"opt":{"idea":"Preorder walk writing '#' for every missing child. Reading tokens back in the same order rebuilds the tree, since each '#' tells us where a subtree ends.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"class Codec:\n    def serialize(self, root):\n        out = []\n\n        def dfs(node):\n            if not node:\n                out.append(\"#\")\n                return\n            out.append(str(node.val))\n            dfs(node.left)\n            dfs(node.right)\n        dfs(root)\n        return \",\".join(out)\n\n    def deserialize(self, data):\n        tokens = iter(data.split(\",\"))\n\n        def build():\n            t = next(tokens)\n            if t == \"#\":\n                return None\n            node = TreeNode(int(t))\n            node.left = build()\n            node.right = build()\n            return node\n        root = build()\n        return root","frames":[{"m":"Write 1","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 2","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 3","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2","#","#","3"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 4","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2","#","#","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 5","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2","#","#","3","4","#","#","5"],"p":{},"hl":[8],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Rebuilt by reading the tokens in the same preorder","l":26,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"rebuilt","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["data","1,2,#,#,3,4,#,#,5,#,#"]]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"rebuilt","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["data","1,2,#,#,3,4,#,#,5,#,#"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"binary-tree-zigzag-level-order-traversal":{"statement":"Return the level order traversal, alternating left→right and right→left.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","[[3], [20, 9], [15, 7]]"],["root = [1]","[[1]]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Plain level order, then reverse every odd level afterwards.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def zigzag_level_order(root):\n    levels, q = [], [root] if root else []\n    while q:\n        levels.append([n.val for n in q])\n        q = [c for n in q for c in (n.left, n.right) if c]\n    return [lv if i % 2 == 0 else lv[::-1] for i, lv in enumerate(levels)]"},"opt":{"idea":"BFS per level, building each level in a deque: append right on even levels, append left on odd levels.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(w)","code":"def zigzag_level_order(root):\n    from collections import deque\n    if not root:\n        return []\n    res, q, ltr = [], deque([root]), True\n    while q:\n        level = deque()\n        for _ in range(len(q)):\n            node = q.popleft()\n            if ltr:\n                level.append(node.val)\n            else:\n                level.appendleft(node.val)\n            if node.left:\n                q.append(node.left)\n            if node.right:\n                q.append(node.right)\n        res.append(list(level))\n        ltr = not ltr\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Level 0 read left → right: [1]","l":17,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 1 read right → left: [3, 2]","l":17,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[4,1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1],[3,2]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 2 read left → right: [4, 5, 6, 7]","l":17,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[2,3,5,6],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1],[3,2],[4,5,6,7]]"]]}]},{"m":"Result: [[1], [3, 2], [4, 5, 6, 7]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[2,3,5,6],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1],[3,2],[4,5,6,7]]"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"count-good-nodes-in-binary-tree":{"statement":"A node is good if no node on the path from the root to it has a greater value. Count good nodes.","examples":[["root = [3, 1, 4, 3, None, 1, 5]","4"],["root = [3, 3, None, 4, 2]","3"],["root = [1]","1"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 1, 4, 3, None, 1, 5]","brute":{"idea":"For each node, find its root path again and check the maximum on it.","tc":"O(n · h)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def good_nodes(root):\n    count = 0\n\n    def visit(n, path):\n        nonlocal count\n        if not n:\n            return\n        if all(v <= n.val for v in path):\n            count += 1\n        visit(n.left, path + [n.val])\n        visit(n.right, path + [n.val])\n    visit(root, [])\n    return count"},"opt":{"idea":"DFS passing the largest value seen so far on the path; a node is good if its value ≥ that max.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def good_nodes(root):\n    good = []\n\n    def dfs(node, high):\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        is_good = node.val >= high\n        if is_good:\n            good.append(node)\n        high = max(high, node.val)\n        return is_good + dfs(node.left, high) + dfs(node.right, high)\n\n    return dfs(root, root.val)","frames":[{"m":"3 vs path max 3 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","1"]]}]},{"m":"1 vs path max 3 → not good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","1"]]}]},{"m":"3 vs path max 3 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[0,2],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","2"]]}]},{"m":"4 vs path max 3 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[0,2,3],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","3"]]}]},{"m":"1 vs path max 4 → not good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[0,2,3],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","3"]]}]},{"m":"5 vs path max 4 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[0,2,3,5],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[0,2,3,5],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","4"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"flatten-binary-tree-to-linked-list":{"statement":"Flatten the tree in place into a 'linked list' along right pointers in preorder; all left pointers become None.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 5, 3, 4, None, 6]","[1, None, 2, None, 3, None, 4, None, 5, None, 6]"],["root = []","[]"],["root = [0]","[0]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 5, 3, 4, None, 6]","brute":{"idea":"Record the preorder nodes in a list, then relink them one after another.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def flatten(root):\n    order = []\n\n    def pre(n):\n        if n:\n            order.append(n)\n            pre(n.left)\n            pre(n.right)\n    pre(root)\n    for a, b in zip(order, order[1:]):\n        a.left, a.right = None, b\n    if order:\n        order[-1].left = order[-1].right = None"},"opt":{"idea":"For each node with a left child: find the rightmost node of the left subtree, hang the right subtree there, move the left subtree to the right. Then step right.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def flatten(root):\n    cur = root\n    while cur:\n        if cur.left:\n            tail = cur.left\n            while tail.right:\n                tail = tail.right\n            tail.right = cur.right\n            cur.right, cur.left = cur.left, None\n        cur = cur.right","frames":[{"m":"At 1: hang its right subtree under 4, then move the left subtree to the right","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,1],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,4],["5",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[3],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 2: hang its right subtree under 3, then move the left subtree to the right","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,1],["2",-1,2],["3",-1,3],["4",-1,4],["5",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: [1, None, 2, None, 3, None, 4, None, 5, None, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,1],["2",-1,2],["3",-1,3],["4",-1,4],["5",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3}},"demo":{"code":"def traversal_demo():\n    root = mk_tree([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, 6])\n    pre, ino, post = [], [], []\n\n    def dfs(node):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        pre.append(node.val)\n        dfs(node.left)\n        ino.append(node.val)\n        dfs(node.right)\n        post.append(node.val)\n\n    dfs(root)\n    return pre, ino, post","frames":[{"m":"Leaving 4: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[2],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 5: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[2,3],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 2: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2,3,1],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 6: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[2,3,1,5],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5","1","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2","6"],"p":{},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 3: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[2,3,1,5,4],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5","1","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2","6","3"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 1: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[2,3,1,5,4,0],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5","1","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2","6","3","1"],"p":{},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"title":"DFS orders: the same tree visited preorder, inorder, postorder"}};
